    V4.06: Cleaned up the code some more and added Style guide compliant
    version string. Also removed a bug (see bugs).

    V4.05: Cleaned up some more code seems to work fine now very stable.

    V4.04: Maintenance test not released.

    New in V4.03: After a request from a user I have added code to create
    a file with the format filename.lzh fullpath:filename.lzh to be used
    as a list of Magic filenames. Currently it will only create this list
    if you use the '-O' overnight switch but I may change this in a future
    release.

    New in V4.00: Rewrote large sections of code and removed several loops
    that were slowing down the execution of the program have now attained
    a speed increase of about 50%


    New in V3.09: Had second thoughts about the header information and
    have now reimplemented them but in a different format. From this
    version onwards if you place a file called 'header.bbs' in any file
    directory this file will get added to your files.bbs file the format
    for this is the same as if you added this information manually to the
    files.bbs see below

\  ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++   
\  ++                                          ++       
\  ++             Amiga Archivers              ++
\  ++                                          ++       
\  ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++

        It is also important not to press return on the last line as
    TransAmiga expects all comment lines to have a '\' in the first
    character position and any variance from this could have unpredictable
    results.

    Removed in V3.09: Removed header information from files.bbs as all
    of the information contained in this is duplicated by the
    filescroll.trans. If anyone really wants this in there files.bbs just
    let me know and I will add it back in for you simple thing to do.
    Removed the '-L' switch and all code associated with it as this has
    now become redundant. From V3.09 onwards a list is created for every
    area in the bulletins directory with the filename being the area
    number.


    New in V3.07: Added the ability to exclude any area from the full list
    I have some other ideas along this line that I am working on and will
    release them when they are ready. Added some code to create a list for
    each area in the same format as full file list. This will allow the
    writing of a short script for use in TransAmiga to create a full list
    and only allowing the user to access areas that they have access for.
    

    New in V3.06: Now has full description in the full files list
    taken from *.desc file. Now has uploaders name in the full file list.
    Cleaned up display so it is easier to see what the program is doing.

